course: dictionary
lesson: 8271
title: Righteous: good and fair
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Righteous means morally right and good: doing what is fair and honest. The Bible says, «The righteous give generously», so a righteous person shares what they have with others.
explain: Look at the words around it. In «Ella stood up for the new girl when the others laughed at her», the action shows what righteous means. Ask: what kind of person would do that? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Words can have more than one meaning. Righteous anger is the anger you feel when something is truly unfair. Self-righteous is different: it means thinking you are better than other people, even when you are not.
fact: Righteous means morally right and good, doing what is fair and honest.
fact: Yad Vashem gives the title «Righteous Among the Nations» to non-Jews who risked their lives to save Jews.
fact: Righteous anger is anger you feel because something is truly unfair.
fact: Self-righteous means thinking you are better than others.
fact: Slang: in the US, some people, in an old-fashioned way, say «righteous» to mean really great or excellent.
exercise: What does righteous mean? | Tired and sleepy | *Morally right and good, doing what is fair and honest | Very rich and powerful | Loud and noisy
exercise: Anger you feel because something is truly unfair is called what? | Sleepy anger | Hungry anger | Silent anger | *Righteous anger
exercise: «He is so self-righteous, he thinks he is better than everyone.» What does self-righteous suggest? | Being kind to everyone | Sleeping well at night | *Thinking you are better than others
test: In the Bible, «the righteous» means which kind of people? | People who are lost | *People who live the way God wants | People who are rich | People who never sleep
test: Which sentence uses righteous in its slang sense? | The judge gave a righteous verdict | The righteous man was poor | *«That skateboard trick was righteous!» | He felt righteous anger at the bully
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to righteous? | Noisy | Careless | *Honest | Greedy
